  "readmeFile": "readme.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v8.4.1 - 2025-10-10\n\t\t\t- Resolved a critical dependency issue that was causing runtime errors in certain environments. This fix ensures that all necessary libraries are correctly referenced and loaded, enhancing the stability and reliability of the framework across diverse deployment scenarios.\n\n\t\t\tv8.4.0 - 2025-10-10\n\t\t\t- Resolved a critical dependency issue that was causing runtime errors in certain environments. This fix ensures that all necessary libraries are correctly referenced and loaded, enhancing the stability and reliability of the framework across diverse deployment scenarios.\n\n\t\t\tv8.3.9 - 2025-06-13\n\t\t\t- Introduced the GetData API in the Job base class. This new protected virtual method allows job implementations to provide custom data retrieval logic,\n\t\t\tenhancing extensibility and enabling more flexible job data sourcing patterns. Job implementations can now override this method to fetch data from various sources and simply return the list.\n\t\t\tNo need to do error handing or calling Save api explicitly.\n\n\t\t\tv8.3.8 - 2025-05-27\n\t\t\t- Getting Trend data with only required fields issue is fixed\n\t\t\t- Example: \thttp://localhost:8011/api/Sales/TrendDataJson/Textiles/Salesman,TotalSales/90\n\t\t\t- This will return only Salesman and TotalSales fields for the last 90 days even though datamodel has more fields",
  "repository": "",
  "requireLicenseAcceptance": true,
